---
layout: base.njk
title: "Addy's Cloud & AI Notes"
home: true
permalink: "/"
---
{%- set alz = collections.topic_alz -%}
{%- macro pill(cx, cy, w, label, i, hot) -%}
<g class="pill{% if hot %} hot{% endif %}" style="--i:{{ i }}"><rect x="{{ cx - w / 2 }}" y="{{ cy - 20 }}" width="{{ w }}" height="40" rx="20"/><text x="{{ cx }}" y="{{ cy }}" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central">{{ label }}</text></g>
{%- endmacro -%}
<section class="band hero">
  <div class="wrap hero-grid">
    <div class="hero-text">
      <p class="chip">Cloud and AI architecture blog</p>
      <h1>From zero to <span class="nb">production-grade</span> cloud and AI architecture.</h1>
      <p class="band-deck">Every post defines its words first, shows one diagram, and points to the lab in the repo. Azure facts are checked against Microsoft Learn.</p>
      <div class="cta">
        <a class="btn amber" href="/start-here/">Start here</a>
        <a class="btn outline" href="#topics">Browse topics</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="hero-art">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 560 440" role="img" aria-label="A cloud at the centre connected to the topics of this blog: Azure Landing Zone, Azure Virtual Desktop, Windows 365, Citrix, AWS, Google Cloud and AI.">
        <defs>
          <radialGradient id="glow" cx="50%" cy="50%" r="50%"><stop offset="0" stop-color="#3C8DF0" stop-opacity=".55"/><stop offset="1" stop-color="#3C8DF0" stop-opacity="0"/></radialGradient>
          <linearGradient id="hg" x1="0" y1="0" x2="1" y2="1"><stop offset="0" stop-color="#9BDAFF"/><stop offset=".55" stop-color="#3C8DF0"/><stop offset="1" stop-color="#1B4FBF"/></linearGradient>
        </defs>
        <circle cx="280" cy="222" r="215" fill="url(#glow)"/>
        <g fill="none" stroke="#8ED0FF" stroke-opacity=".12"><circle cx="280" cy="222" r="105"/><circle cx="280" cy="222" r="165"/><circle cx="280" cy="222" r="215"/></g>
        <g class="wires" fill="none" stroke="#8ED0FF" stroke-opacity=".55" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-dasharray="4 7">
          <line x1="280" y1="222" x2="280" y2="38"/><line x1="280" y1="222" x2="425" y2="111"/><line x1="280" y1="222" x2="463" y2="264"/><line x1="280" y1="222" x2="360" y2="374"/><line x1="280" y1="222" x2="200" y2="374"/><line x1="280" y1="222" x2="96" y2="264"/><line x1="280" y1="222" x2="134" y2="111"/>
        </g>
        <g transform="translate(195 172) scale(3.7)">
          <path d="M38.5 27H12a9 9 0 0 1-1.6-17.86A12 12 0 0 1 33.6 8.4 10 10 0 0 1 38.5 27Z" fill="url(#hg)"/>
          <path d="M16.2 23.2 23 7.8l6.8 15.4M18.9 18h8.2" fill="none" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="2.3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
          <path class="spark" d="M33.5 3.5l1 2.6 2.6 1-2.6 1-1 2.6-1-2.6-2.6-1 2.6-1z" fill="#FFB000"/>
        </g>
        {{ pill(280, 38, 64, "AI", 0, false) }}
        {{ pill(425, 111, 252, "Azure Virtual Desktop", 1, false) }}
        {{ pill(463, 264, 150, "Windows 365", 2, false) }}
        {{ pill(360, 374, 98, "Citrix", 3, false) }}
        {{ pill(200, 374, 70, "AWS", 4, false) }}
        {{ pill(96, 264, 160, "Google Cloud", 5, false) }}
        {{ pill(134, 111, 224, "Azure Landing Zone", 6, true) }}
      </svg>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section-pad" id="topics"><div class="wrap">
  <h2 class="sh">Browse by topic</h2>
  <p class="lead">Pick a topic to see all of its posts.</p>
  <div class="tiles">
  {%- for t in topics %}
    {%- set n = collections["topic_" + t.tag].length %}
    <a class="tile{% if not n %} soon{% endif %}" href="/{{ t.slug }}/">
      <span class="tile-ico">{% set g = t.glyph %}{% include "glyph.njk" %}</span>
      <span class="tile-name">{{ t.name }}</span>
      <span class="tile-text">{{ t.blurb | clip(88) }}</span>
      <span class="tile-state">{% if n %}{{ n }} posts{% else %}Coming soon{% endif %}</span>
    </a>
  {%- endfor %}
  </div>
</div></section>

<section class="section-pad alt"><div class="wrap">
  <div class="sh-row"><h2 class="sh">Latest posts</h2><a class="all" href="/azure-landing-zone/">All Azure Landing Zone posts</a></div>
  <div class="plist">
  {%- set tp = topics | topicByTag(["alz"]) %}
  {%- for p in alz | latest(5) %}{% include "card.njk" %}{% endfor %}
  </div>
</div></section>

<section class="section-pad"><div class="wrap">
  <h2 class="sh">How each post is built</h2>
  <p class="lead">Every post has the same six parts, so you always know where to look.</p>
  <ol class="steps">
    <li><b>The problem</b><span>What the topic solves.</span></li>
    <li><b>A plain explanation</b><span>It starts with the words you need first.</span></li>
    <li><b>One diagram</b><span>Simplified, with the Microsoft Learn page named.</span></li>
    <li><b>What I have seen in production</b><span>And which mistakes to check for first.</span></li>
    <li><b>The repo file</b><span>The lab or reference that goes with the post.</span></li>
    <li><b>Sources</b><span>Up to three Microsoft Learn pages.</span></li>
  </ol>
</div></section>
